# Rulebook and cost-config files are identified by SHA-256 of their content, recorded on every
# desk decision for exact replay. core.autocrlf (set true on this checkout) would otherwise let
# the SAME committed content check out as LF on one machine and CRLF on another, changing the hash
# of "the same file" depending on checkout settings alone. Forcing eol=lf here means git always
# checks these out with LF regardless of core.autocrlf -- desk/lib/rulebook.py and desk/lib/costs.py
# additionally normalize CRLF->LF before hashing, so the hash is stable even for a file that was
# already checked out or edited with CRLF before this rule existed.
rulebook/* text eol=lf
config/* text eol=lf
